<title>BANGLADESH: Bangladesh GQ Ball Pen '95 net profit up 15.3 pct.</title>
<headline>Bangladesh GQ Ball Pen '95 net profit up 15.3 pct.</headline>
<text>
<p>DHAKA, Sept 25 (Rueter) - The year ended on December 31, 1995</p>
<p>(In million taka unless stated)</p>
<p>				    1995		1994</p>
<p>    Net sale		    372.32   vs     328.3</p>
<p>    Gross profit		 66.08   vs	63.17</p>
<p>    Net profit before tax    41.90   vs	41.54</p>
<p>    Net profit after tax     30.12   vs	26.12</p>
<p>    Dividend		     55 percent vs 45 percent</p>
<p>Note: The company, which announced its results on Wednesday, said it could reduce the production cost in the year by using waste plastic. It also offered one bonus share for two shares.</p>
</text>
